[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2724520585","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104085#issuecomment-2724520585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104085","id":2724520585,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iZOKJ","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-14T12:21:15Z","updated_at":"2025-03-14T12:21:15Z","body":"This is the intended behavior, and applies to Godot Physics too.\n\nThe `physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread` project setting does not make everything physics-related run on a separate thread. The physics thread will still synchronize with the main thread for the duration of `_physics_process` and `_integrate_forces`, which indeed are still run on the main thread.\n\nThe main benefit of `physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread` is that the physics engine can be stepped after this synchronization while the rest of the engine iteration is happening, meaning you'll be running next frame's simulation in parallel with (for example) `_process` being called.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2724520585/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784183169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104085#issuecomment-2784183169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104085","id":2784183169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l80OB","user":{"login":"RonYanDaik","id":3350340,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNTAzNDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3350340?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik","html_url":"https://github.com/RonYanDaik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonYanDaik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T18:15:45Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T18:15:45Z","body":"> The physics thread will still synchronize with the main thread for the duration of `_physics_process` and `_integrate_forces`, which indeed are still run on the main thread.\n\nwas it always like this?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784183169/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"per